{
 "cells": [
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "template-intro",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Gen 1 / OS 2 field-test starter\n",
    "\n",
    "For a new checkout, copy this template to test.ipynb and edit the hostname. Run the steps in order. test.ipynb is ignored by Git so your settings and results stay local."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "template-local-note",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 1. Select the board and image\n",
    "\n",
    "Edit the hostname. This cell only checks which local PyRPL installation and fork bitstream will be used."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "template-local",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import json\n",
    "from pathlib import Path\n",
    "import sys\n",
    "\n",
    "import pyrpl\n",
    "from pyrpl.redpitaya import RedPitaya\n",
    "\n",
    "HOSTNAME = \"rp-xxxxxx.local\"\n",
    "SSH_USER = \"root\"\n",
    "bitstream = Path(pyrpl.__file__).resolve().parent / \"fpga\" / \"red_pitaya.bin\"\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Python:\", sys.executable)\n",
    "print(\"PyRPL:\", pyrpl.__file__)\n",
    "print(\"Bitstream:\", bitstream)\n",
    "assert bitstream.is_file()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "template-preflight-note",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 2. Run the read-only preflight\n",
    "\n",
    "Enter the SSH password. This checks the OS, board profile, overlay contract, and local FPGA files without uploading or programming anything."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "template-preflight",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "from getpass import getpass\n",
    "\n",
    "SSH_PASSWORD = getpass(\"SSH password: \")\n",
    "device = None\n",
    "try:\n",
    "    device = RedPitaya(\n",
    "        config=None,\n",
    "        hostname=HOSTNAME,\n",
    "        user=SSH_USER,\n",
    "        password=SSH_PASSWORD,\n",
    "        gui=False,\n",
    "        autostart=False,\n",
    "        reloadfpga=False,\n",
    "        reloadserver=False,\n",
    "    )\n",
    "    preflight_report = device.preflight_fpga_update(filename=str(bitstream))\n",
    "finally:\n",
    "    if device is not None:\n",
    "        device.end_ssh()\n",
    "\n",
    "print(json.dumps(preflight_report, indent=2, sort_keys=True))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "template-program-note",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 3. Program the FPGA\n",
    "\n",
    "This uploads the fork BIN and matching DTBO and programs the FPGA. It does not start the PyRPL server. Use only on the intended original Z7010 board."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "template-program",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "device = None\n",
    "try:\n",
    "    device = RedPitaya(\n",
    "        config=None,\n",
    "        hostname=HOSTNAME,\n",
    "        user=SSH_USER,\n",
    "        password=SSH_PASSWORD,\n",
    "        filename=str(bitstream),\n",
    "        gui=False,\n",
    "        autostart=False,\n",
    "        reloadfpga=False,\n",
    "        reloadserver=False,\n",
    "    )\n",
    "    program_report = device.update_fpga(filename=str(bitstream))\n",
    "finally:\n",
    "    if device is not None:\n",
    "        device.end_ssh()\n",
    "\n",
    "print(json.dumps(program_report, indent=2, sort_keys=True))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "template-connect-note",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 4. Start PyRPL and connect\n",
    "\n",
    "This installs/starts the monitor server and checks the fork register map. It does not reprogram the FPGA."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "template-connect",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "from pyrpl import Pyrpl\n",
    "\n",
    "p = Pyrpl(\n",
    "    config=\"gen1-os2-field-test\",\n",
    "    hostname=HOSTNAME,\n",
    "    user=SSH_USER,\n",
    "    password=SSH_PASSWORD,\n",
    "    filename=str(bitstream),\n",
    "    gui=False,\n",
    "    reloadfpga=False,\n",
    "    reloadserver=True,\n",
    ")\n",
    "rp = p.rp\n",
    "print(\"PyRPL connected; fork register checks passed.\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "template-read-note",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 5. Read a module setting\n",
    "\n",
    "This reads PID0's input-filter setting without driving an output. Further analog/control checks require their own measurements."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "template-read",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "print(\"PID0 input filter:\", rp.pid0.inputfilter)"
   ]
  }
